      "note": "Building at launchers/superclaude:210-234. The spawn is parented on the CALLER'S cgroup: setsid detaches the tty and not the cgroup, so the one resident process in the system dies with whatever window launched it — measured twice (2026-08-10 reboot, 2026-08-18 Konsole scope oom-kill). It becomes a transient user unit (systemd-run --user --unit), a SIBLING of the caller's scope, guarded by the same probe+fall-through shape the memory scope 60 lines below already uses. MEASURED AT CHART AND IT CHANGED THE BUILD: a transient unit that exits NONZERO stays loaded in `failed` state and blocks its own name, and the singleton loser exits 3 BY DESIGN — so the naive change would wedge the unit name on the first losing launch and every later launch would silently fail to start the loop. SuccessExitStatus=3 plus a blind reset-failed (measured harmless on a live unit) close it. Chart chain: seven berths, validate at /home/akien/.cairn/devices/chart/0/packets/validate-20260818T160010-a6527557b941.json. The proof is written FIRST and run against the unmodified launcher, because a proof that has never seen the failure it grips is how a hollow green is bought.",
